The timetable can’t be finished because several lab courses have far fewer qualified teachers than needed. Each of these labs runs three batches at the same time for different student sections, but only two (or in a couple of cases one) teachers are currently qualified to run them. The system can’t assign staff for the missing slots, so the schedule is blocked.

**What’s happening (by subject and section)**  
- Computer Networks Lab (SEC III A) – 3 batches, only 2 teachers.  
- Internship (SEC III A) – 3 batches, only 2 teachers.  
- Data Base Management Systems Lab (SEC III B) – 3 batches, only 2 teachers.  
- Object Oriented Programming Systems Lab (SEC II A) – 3 batches, only 2 teachers.  
- Computer Architecture Lab (SEC II A) – 3 batches, only 2 teachers.  
- Agile Software Methodology Lab (SEC II B) – 3 batches, only 2 teachers.  
- Mobile App Development Lab (SEC II B) – 3 batches, only 2 teachers.  
- Internship (SEC IV A) – 3 batches, only 1 teacher.  
- Internship (SEC IV B) – 3 batches, only 1 teacher.

**Suggested action**  
For each of these courses, add at least one more qualified teacher so that the minimum of three teachers matches the three simultaneous batches. Once we have the required staffing, the timetable can be generated normally.

